  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When three Central Continent Immortal Gu Houses pierce the heavenly wind qi wall into black heaven, Combat Immortal Sect’s Edge Link Camp stands with Wind Cloud Manor’s Wind Sweeping Building and Heavenly Lotus Sect’s Canary Pavilion. It leads at the front and opens the path: giant sharp horns form as solid figures and stab through the heavenly wind qi wall to force a tunnel. Halfway through, it loses many Gu worms, its charging power falls, and it rotates to the back while the other two houses take front duty in turn.",
      "chapters": [
        1239
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "fac_combat_immortal_sect",
        "house_wind_cloud_manor",
        "house_wind_sweeping_building",
        "fac_heavenly_lotus_sect",
        "house_canary_pavilion",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Against a night heavenly wolf group, Edge Link Camp opens the path again: its aura rises as immortal essence is expended rapidly and a huge charging horn pierces the wolf formation.",
      "chapters": [
        1242
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battles-in-the-crossing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After a star cloud storm, Edge Link Camp and Canary Pavilion are heavily damaged inside a sky chief encirclement; Edge Link Camp then bursts with sharp horn silhouettes that even ancient sky chiefs dare not take head on.",
      "chapters": [
        1246
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "battles-in-the-crossing",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "South Desolation Immortal remembers Edge Link Camp as the strongest of the three Central Continent Immortal Gu Houses and then learns it has appeared above Snowy Mountain blessed land. Its power is extremely high with two rank eight Gu Immortals, Wei Ling Yang and Bi Chen Tian, controlling it; giant horn shadows bombard Snowy Mountain while it contends with the fate reversing sacrificial refinement formation.",
      "chapters": [
        1267
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "snowy-mountain-campaign",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_south_desolation_immortal",
        "loc_snowy_mountain",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "char_wei_ling_yang",
        "char_bi_chen_tian"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When those rank eights leave to attack weak points, rank seven Gu Immortals keep Edge Link Camp as a defensive turtle shell that refuses fatal openings for a time.",
      "chapters": [
        1269
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "snowy-mountain-campaign",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reverse Flow River later engulfs Edge Link Camp, and the house breaks apart in the river.",
      "chapters": [
        1271
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "snowy-mountain-campaign",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_reverse_flow_river"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Central Continent had temporarily placed Affection Immortal Gu with many mortal Gu in Edge Link Camp so the house could track love Gu even inside an immortal aperture, which is how it found Snowy Mountain; those Gu are swept away when the house breaks.",
      "chapters": [
        1273
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "snowy-mountain-campaign",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_affection_immortal_gu",
        "sys_mortal_gu",
        "gu_love_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "After that destruction, Central Continent’s group is treated as even more disadvantaged if it fights again.",
      "chapters": [
        1274
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "snowy-mountain-campaign",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Deviation (recorded): this page is filed under gu-houses because Edge Link Camp is a named Immortal Gu House. It is mobile equipment of Combat Immortal Sect, not a five-region map seat.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "snowy-mountain-campaign",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ye Fan later names Combat Immortal Sect’s Edge Link Camp among Immortal Gu Houses floating over Emperor City, still with grand flags fluttering.",
      "chapters": [
        1931
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reappearance-over-emperor-city",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ye_fan",
        "loc_emperor_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In that battlefield Edge Link Camp rushes Fang clan’s Inquiry Dock and uses the killer move Giant Horn Rush, a giant horn of condensed light; under heroes among people that rush roughly doubles in power, and Inquiry Dock alone cannot resist it.",
      "chapters": [
        1933
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "reappearance-over-emperor-city",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_fang_clan",
        "house_inquiry_dock",
        "move_giant_horn_rush"
      ]
    }
  ],
